.TH BIOKIDS\-VOICE 1 2026\-09\-30 "biokids 0.1.0" "BioKids"
.SH NAME
biokids\-voice \- Zio and Sio, the BioKids voices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biokids\-voice
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-audio ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biokids\-voice
speaks to the child: a welcome, and the warnings before time runs out.
Each line is also shown on screen as a card.
Speech is made on the machine, with
.BR espeak\-ng (1)
unless the family has installed Piper; nothing is sent anywhere.
A parent can download Piper and its Turkish voice with one button in the
panel, which runs
.BR "biokids\-admin voice\-setup" ;
the program is then used from
.IR /var/lib/biokids\-voices/piper/ ,
and one on the PATH otherwise.
It runs in the child's own session as the systemd user unit
.BR biokids\-voice.service ;
the child's session starts it, not a person.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the configuration from
.I file
instead of
.IR /etc/biokids/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Listen on
.I path
instead of the configured socket.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Show the cards but play nothing, for a machine with no sound card.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/biokids/voice/
What Zio and Sio say, one file per event and language.
.TP
.I /var/lib/biokids\-voices/models/piper/
Piper voices:
.IB locale \- persona .onnx
with its
.B .onnx.json
beside it, such as
.IR tr\-sio.onnx .
When Zio's is the same file as Sio's, she speaks it higher.
.TP
.I /var/lib/biokids\-voices/piper/
The Piper program the panel downloaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR biokids\-admin (8),
.BR biokids\-shell (1),
.BR espeak\-ng (1)
